From: BashKitten contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Discover extensions from the existing native user preset

The released server installs UserSettings extensions and sends
userpresetconfigid, but the browser loader only fetches the built-in and shared
preset indexes. Reuse its existing preset loader for the native user stream,
after shared settings so the existing per-ID merge preserves user precedence.
No new extension protocol, authorization or preset storage is introduced.

--- a/browser/src/control/Control.Extension.ts
+++ b/browser/src/control/Control.Extension.ts
@@ -2340,6 +2340,7 @@ window.L.loadExtensions = async function (map: any, docType: string) {
 	const builtinIds = await fetchIndex('extensions/');
 	sources.push({ baseRel: 'extensions/', ids: builtinIds });
 	if (app.presetConfigId) await addPresetSource(app.presetConfigId);
+	if (app.userPresetConfigId) await addPresetSource(app.userPresetConfigId);
 
 	// Flatten the sources into one list of (id, baseRel) entries; Map.set's last-write-wins
 	// behavior causes admin extensions to override built-in
